---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="BulkMagic — Streamlining Multi-State Seller Onboarding" theme="light">
<!-- Luminous Gallery Atmosphere: Layered Warm Ambient Gradients -->
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-20 bg-[#FAF9F5]"></div>
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-20 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_75%_55%_at_70%_10%,rgba(217,119,6,0.045),transparent_65%)]"></div>
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-20 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_60%_45%_at_15%_25%,rgba(13,148,136,0.035),transparent_60%)]"></div>
<div class="fixed inset-0 pointer-events-none -z-20 bg-[radial-gradient(ellipse_55%_40%_at_85%_75%,rgba(217,119,6,0.03),transparent_70%)]"></div>

<main id="main" class="relative max-w-page mx-auto px-6 md:px-16 lg:px-20 pb-72 pt-20 md:pt-32 font-sans text-neutral-800 selection:bg-amber-500/20 selection:text-neutral-900">

  <!-- HERO SECTION: Grounded Headline & Sprint Scope -->
  <section class="mb-32 md:mb-44">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mb-16">
      <h1 class="font-serif text-5xl sm:text-7xl lg:text-[6.25rem] font-normal leading-[0.94] tracking-[-0.04em] text-neutral-950 mb-10 text-balance">
        Designing Multi-State Merchant Onboarding.
      </h1>
      <p class="text-2xl sm:text-3xl text-neutral-800 font-normal leading-snug tracking-tight mb-12 max-w-[50ch]">
        Simplifying legal compliance so new merchants can get approved and start selling, fast.
      </p>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-[1.3fr_0.7fr] gap-12 lg:gap-24 items-start pt-6 border-t border-neutral-200">
        <div>
          <p class="text-xl sm:text-2xl text-neutral-800 font-normal leading-[1.75] max-w-[52ch] text-pretty">
            To get merchants selling quickly, onboarding needs to respect their time. In a rapid day-and-a-half sprint, I designed an adaptive onboarding flow that asks only for what is necessary for a seller's business structure, supports multi-session document collection, and built an AI-assisted prototype to validate the interaction model.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Margin Ledger: Pure High-Signal Coordinates (Zero Redundancy) -->
        <div class="lg:pt-2 pl-0 lg:pl-10">
          <dl class="space-y-5 text-xs font-mono">
            <div>
              <dt class="text-neutral-500 text-[10px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase mb-1 font-medium">MY ROLE</dt>
              <dd class="text-neutral-950 text-sm font-medium">Product &amp; Interaction Designer</dd>
            </div>
            <div>
              <dt class="text-neutral-500 text-[10px] tracking-[0.22em] uppercase mb-1 font-medium">DELIVERABLES</dt>
              <dd class="text-neutral-950 text-sm font-medium">Compliance Architecture &amp; AI-Generated Prototype</dd>
            </div>
          </dl>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Hero Stepped Interaction Deck: Cascading Overlap Stage -->
    <figure class="pt-8 border-t border-neutral-200">
      <div class="relative py-4 sm:py-8 overflow-hidden lg:overflow-visible">
        <!-- Horizontal stage that cascades on desktop, smoothly scrolls on mobile -->
        <div class="flex items-center justify-start lg:justify-center overflow-x-auto lg:overflow-visible no-scrollbar -mx-6 px-6 sm:-mx-16 sm:px-16 lg:mx-0 lg:px-0 py-8">
          
          <!-- Viewport 01: Entity Identification -->
          <div class="relative shrink-0 w-[270px] sm:w-[310px] md:w-[330px] lg:w-[350px] aspect-[10/16] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800/80 bg-[#0E1117] shadow-[0_16px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12)] z-[1] hover:z-[20] hover:-translate-y-4 hover:scale-[1.02] hover:shadow-[0_28px_60px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] transition-luxury cursor-default">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/business-info(1).png"
              alt="Mobile viewport: Business structure and entity identification"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top block"
              loading="eager"
            />
          </div>

          <!-- Viewport 02: Document Preparation Checklist -->
          <div class="relative shrink-0 w-[270px] sm:w-[310px] md:w-[330px] lg:w-[350px] aspect-[10/16] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800/80 bg-[#0E1117] shadow-[0_16px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12)] -ml-16 sm:-ml-20 md:-ml-24 lg:-ml-24 z-[2] hover:z-[20] hover:-translate-y-4 hover:scale-[1.02] hover:shadow-[0_28px_60px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] transition-luxury cursor-default">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/document-preparation(1).png"
              alt="Mobile viewport: Dynamic document readiness checklist"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top block"
              loading="eager"
            />
          </div>

          <!-- Viewport 03: Tax Details & Nexus -->
          <div class="relative shrink-0 w-[270px] sm:w-[310px] md:w-[330px] lg:w-[350px] aspect-[10/16] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800/80 bg-[#0E1117] shadow-[0_16px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12)] -ml-16 sm:-ml-20 md:-ml-24 lg:-ml-24 z-[3] hover:z-[20] hover:-translate-y-4 hover:scale-[1.02] hover:shadow-[0_28px_60px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] transition-luxury cursor-default">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/tax-details(1).png"
              alt="Mobile viewport: Tax nexus and compliance details"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top block"
              loading="eager"
            />
          </div>

          <!-- Viewport 04: Banking Details -->
          <div class="relative shrink-0 w-[270px] sm:w-[310px] md:w-[330px] lg:w-[350px] aspect-[10/16] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800/80 bg-[#0E1117] shadow-[0_16px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12)] -ml-16 sm:-ml-20 md:-ml-24 lg:-ml-24 z-[4] hover:z-[20] hover:-translate-y-4 hover:scale-[1.02] hover:shadow-[0_28px_60px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] transition-luxury cursor-default">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/banking-details(1).png"
              alt="Mobile viewport: Direct deposit and payout verification"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top block"
              loading="eager"
            />
          </div>

          <!-- Viewport 05: Activation & Review -->
          <div class="relative shrink-0 w-[270px] sm:w-[310px] md:w-[330px] lg:w-[350px] aspect-[10/16] rounded-2xl overflow-hidden border border-neutral-800/80 bg-[#0E1117] shadow-[0_16px_40px_rgba(0,0,0,0.12)] -ml-16 sm:-ml-20 md:-ml-24 lg:-ml-24 z-[5] hover:z-[20] hover:-translate-y-4 hover:scale-[1.02] hover:shadow-[0_28px_60px_rgba(0,0,0,0.22)] transition-luxury cursor-default">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/onboarding-success(1).png"
              alt="Mobile viewport: Account review and live activation"
              class="w-full h-full object-cover object-top block"
              loading="eager"
            />
          </div>

        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-4 border-t border-neutral-200 pt-3 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center justify-between gap-2">
        <span>5-Stage Merchant Onboarding Architecture</span>
        <span class="text-neutral-500 font-normal">Sequential Viewport Progression · Business Entity to Live Activation</span>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <!-- THE CONSTRAINT -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-y border-neutral-200 mb-28 md:mb-36">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-neutral-950 leading-[1.06] tracking-tight font-normal text-balance">
        42 legal questions stood between a new seller and their first sale.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 font-normal text-lg leading-[1.8] max-w-[54ch]">
        <p class="text-neutral-950 font-normal text-xl leading-relaxed">
          Marketplaces can't bypass compliance. Federal and state laws strictly require verifying identities, collecting W-9 tax forms, and tracking sales tax obligations across every operating jurisdiction. When you compile the full checklist of potential legal requirements across all business entity types, it totals 42 separate questions and filings.
        </p>
        <p>
          Standard compliance portals approach this by presenting all 42 questions as a monolithic form. For an independent merchant, that creates immediate cognitive overload and hesitation.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE DISCOVERY -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-b border-neutral-200 mb-28 md:mb-36">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-neutral-950 leading-[1.06] tracking-tight font-normal text-balance">
        Most compliance questions don't apply to every seller.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 font-normal text-lg leading-[1.8] max-w-[54ch]">
        <p class="text-neutral-950 font-normal text-xl leading-relaxed">
          Auditing the statutory requirements revealed that 28 of the 42 requirements—such as Articles of Incorporation, board resolutions, and complex multi-state foreign qualifications—apply strictly to C-Corps and multi-tier corporate entities.
        </p>
        <p>
          For a sole proprietor or single-member LLC, these questions create unnecessary friction. The friction wasn't compliance itself—it was asking sellers to parse rules that don't apply to them.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- THE ADAPTIVE ARCHITECTURE -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-b border-neutral-200 mb-32 md:mb-40">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6 mb-16">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-neutral-950 leading-[1.06] tracking-tight font-normal text-balance">
        Reducing cognitive load through adaptive disclosure.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-neutral-700 font-normal text-lg leading-[1.8] max-w-[54ch]">
        <p class="text-neutral-950 font-normal text-xl leading-relaxed">
          The solution was to make the flow adaptive. Asking two foundational questions first—business structure and location—immediately filters the requirements, presenting only the 14 items relevant to that seller's business.
        </p>
        <p>
          Because gathering tax documents often takes time, the flow supports multi-session completion. A transparent checklist shows required files, validation status, and lets sellers save and return at their own pace without losing progress.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- The Adaptive Contrast Vitrine: Monolithic Burden vs Tailored Path -->
    <div class="border-t border-neutral-200 pt-10 space-y-8">
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
        <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-wider text-neutral-600 font-medium">Compliance Architecture Comparison</span>
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-neutral-500">42 Statutory Requirements vs 14 Tailored Fields</span>
      </div>

      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 lg:gap-12 items-start">
        
        <!-- Left: The Monolithic Regulatory Burden (Ghosted & De-emphasized) -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-5 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 border-b border-neutral-200">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-neutral-500 uppercase tracking-wider">Monolithic Intake Form</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-neutral-500">42 questions</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-600 leading-normal">
            Standard platforms present every possible statutory question regardless of entity size, burying small merchants under irrelevant legal filings.
          </p>

          <!-- Ghosted Wireframe Grid of 42 Items -->
          <div class="p-5 rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/80 bg-neutral-100/50 space-y-2.5">
            <div class="font-mono text-[10px] text-neutral-400 uppercase tracking-widest pb-1 border-b border-neutral-200/60">
              Exhaustive Regulatory Matrix
            </div>
            <div class="grid grid-cols-2 gap-x-3 gap-y-1.5 font-mono text-[11px] text-neutral-400/80 leading-tight">
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Articles of Org.</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Foreign Qual. Cert.</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Beneficial Ownership</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Franchise Tax ID</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Director Resolution</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Secondary Officer ID</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Multi-State Resale</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">UCC-1 Financing</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Bylaws Attestation</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Nexus Determination</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Share Registry</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Corporate Seal Aff.</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">State Withholding</span>
              <span class="truncate line-through decoration-neutral-300">Excise Tax Permit</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pt-2 border-t border-neutral-200/60 flex items-center justify-between text-[11px] font-mono text-neutral-500">
              <span>+ 28 corporate requirements</span>
              <span class="text-neutral-400">Omitted</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Right: The BulkMagic Adaptive Path (High-Contrast, Distilled Clarity) -->
        <div class="lg:col-span-7 space-y-4">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between pb-2 border-b border-neutral-950/20">
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-neutral-950 uppercase tracking-wider font-semibold">BulkMagic Adaptive Path</span>
            <span class="font-mono text-xs text-amber-800 font-semibold">14 tailored fields (−67%)</span>
          </div>
          <p class="text-sm text-neutral-700 leading-normal">
            By establishing business structure and active states in the first step, questions are filtered to only what applies. Sellers can complete them across sessions.
          </p>

          <!-- Tailored 14-Step Micro-Ledger -->
          <div class="p-6 rounded-xl border border-neutral-200 bg-white shadow-xs space-y-5">
            <div class="space-y-4">
              <!-- Stage 1 -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between font-mono text-[11px] pb-1 border-b border-neutral-100">
                  <span class="font-medium text-neutral-950">1. Entity &amp; Presence</span>
                  <span class="text-neutral-500">3 fields</span>
                </div>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 pt-2 text-xs text-neutral-700">
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Business Structure</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Primary State</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">DBA / Trade Name</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- Stage 2 -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between font-mono text-[11px] pb-1 border-b border-neutral-100">
                  <span class="font-medium text-neutral-950">2. Tax Identification &amp; Nexus</span>
                  <span class="text-neutral-500">4 fields</span>
                </div>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-2 pt-2 text-xs text-neutral-700">
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Federal EIN</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">State Sales Tax ID</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Resale Permit</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Tax Exemption</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- Stage 3 -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between font-mono text-[11px] pb-1 border-b border-neutral-100">
                  <span class="font-medium text-neutral-950">3. Payout Verification &amp; Identity</span>
                  <span class="text-neutral-500">4 fields</span>
                </div>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-2 pt-2 text-xs text-neutral-700">
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Routing Number</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Account Number</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Gov. Issued ID</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Proof of Address</span>
                </div>
              </div>

              <!-- Stage 4 -->
              <div>
                <div class="flex items-baseline justify-between font-mono text-[11px] pb-1 border-b border-neutral-100">
                  <span class="font-medium text-neutral-950">4. Review &amp; Activation</span>
                  <span class="text-neutral-500">3 fields</span>
                </div>
                <div class="grid grid-cols-3 gap-2 pt-2 text-xs text-neutral-700">
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Terms Attestation</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px]">Authorized Signature</span>
                  <span class="bg-neutral-50 border border-neutral-200/60 rounded px-2.5 py-1.5 font-mono text-[11px] text-amber-800 font-medium">Instant Submission</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Multi-Session Progress Footer -->
            <div class="pt-3 border-t border-neutral-100 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-between text-xs font-mono text-neutral-600 gap-2">
              <span class="flex items-center gap-1.5">
                <span class="w-1.5 h-1.5 rounded-full bg-emerald-600"></span>
                Multi-session auto-save enabled
              </span>
              <span class="text-neutral-500">Field syntax checked live</span>
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- INTERACTION WALKTHROUGH -->
  <section class="mb-48 md:mb-56">
    <div class="space-y-36 md:space-y-48">

      <!-- ENTITY CLASSIFICATION & ROUTING -->
      <article class="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-balance">
            Setting the Rules Based on Business Structure
          </h3>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-[54ch]">
            The onboarding begins with two straightforward questions: business structure and operating states. Answering this upfront sets the rules for the rest of the flow, ensuring sellers only see the filings required for their specific entity type.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/progressive-disclosure.png"
              alt="Business structure identification and progressive disclosure routing interface"
              class="w-full h-auto object-contain block"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-3">
            Step-by-step business structure identification &amp; routing
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <!-- DYNAMIC REQUIREMENTS CHECKLIST -->
      <article class="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-balance">
            A Transparent Checklist Supporting Multi-Session Progress
          </h3>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-[54ch]">
            Sellers rarely have every tax certificate or resale permit on hand right away. Instead of surprising them mid-flow with unexpected file requests, a structured checklist outlines the required documents, clearly tracks validation status (Ready, Pending, Missing), and lets sellers save and return across multiple sessions without losing progress.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/document-checklist.png"
              alt="Dynamic document checklist adapting in real time to entity type and location"
              class="w-full h-auto object-contain block"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-3">
            Document readiness checklist with transparent validation status
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <!-- FIELD VALIDATION & ERROR PREVENTION -->
      <article class="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-balance">
            Field-Level Validation to Catch Errors at the Source
          </h3>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-[54ch]">
            Rather than letting typos in tax IDs or misformatted bank details trigger failed submissions days later, form fields validate syntax and formatting as the seller types. Clear inline prompts guide corrections immediately, ensuring the application is clean before final submission.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/automated-validation.png"
              alt="Real-time inline syntax validation and economic nexus threshold checks"
              class="w-full h-auto object-contain block"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-3">
            Instant syntax and formatting checks on typed business details
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

      <!-- TRANSPARENT REVIEW & ACTIVATION -->
      <article class="space-y-8">
        <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-4">
          <h3 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-4xl lg:text-[2.75rem] text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-[1.1] tracking-tight text-balance">
            In-Place Edits Before Final Activation
          </h3>
          <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-relaxed max-w-[54ch]">
            A single summary screen confirms registered details, tax nexuses, and bank payout information in a clean ledger. Sellers can edit details directly in place without clicking "back" through multiple screens, leading immediately into active selling.
          </p>
        </div>

        <figure>
          <div class="rounded-xl border border-neutral-200/90 bg-white shadow-xs overflow-hidden">
            <img
              src="/assets/bulkmagic/onboarding-success.png"
              alt="Account activation confirmation and success screen"
              class="w-full h-auto object-contain block"
              loading="lazy"
            />
          </div>
          <figcaption class="text-[11px] font-mono tracking-wider text-neutral-600 uppercase mt-3">
            Account activation confirmation and live status review
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- SPRINT REFLECTION -->
  <section class="py-20 md:py-28 border-y border-neutral-200 mb-36 md:mb-48">
    <div class="max-w-4xl space-y-6">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl sm:text-5xl text-neutral-950 font-normal leading-tight">
        Rapid prototyping as a compliance stress-test.
      </h2>
      <div class="space-y-5 text-base sm:text-lg text-neutral-700 font-normal leading-[1.8] max-w-[54ch]">
        <p>
          In a rapid sprint spanning roughly 36 hours, the goal was to take dense statutory regulations and prove that compliance doesn't have to be a multi-week engineering project before you can validate the experience. Using AI to generate a functional prototype allowed me to stress-test state transitions, uncover edge cases, and capture realistic UI states in hours rather than weeks.
        </p>
        <p class="text-neutral-800">
          If moving to a production build, the immediate next steps would be running usability sessions with active sellers to test document gathering across multiple sessions, tracking completion drop-off, and collaborating with engineering on realistic document verification pipelines.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- CHAPTER NAVIGATION -->
  <section class="pt-16 border-t border-neutral-200">
    <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row items-baseline justify-between gap-12 font-mono text-xs">
